        "detailed_text":  "Week 0 served as the orientation and foundation phase of PRICE ProtoSem, introducing participants to the programme structure and to one another before the 20-week retail problem-solving journey began.\n\nDay 1: The week opened with introductions â€” to fellow participants, the programme itself, and what would be expected over the coming weeks. This was followed by icebreaker activities designed to help everyone get comfortable with the group.\n\nDay 2: Sessions covered building a professional presence on LinkedIn, a self-understanding exercise through the 16Personalities assessment, and short story presentations that encouraged creativity and communication.\n\nDay 3: Story presentations continued, alongside an ITEC TechTalk. The day also included team-based activities â€” Imposter, Challenge, and Marshmello â€” aimed at building interaction, collaboration, and problem-solving skills.\n\nDay 4: Featured a TechTalk on the Art of Prompting, an orientation covering the programme roadmap and what lay ahead, an introduction to the leaderboard system, and the official inauguration of ProtoSem.\n\nBeta Teams: For Week 0, participants were grouped into temporary \"Beta Teams.\" Working with a different set of people gave everyone a chance to interact, collaborate, and experience teamwork before permanent team structures were set.\n\nFriday â€” Entrepreneurship Day: The morning featured a session led by an industry expert, followed by an afternoon reflection session where participants reviewed the week\u0027s activities and takeaways.\n\nOverall, Week 0 functioned as a foundation-building week â€” helping participants connect with each other, understand the programme, explore different skills, and prepare for the real-world retail challenges ahead.",
