        "status":  "documented",
        "detailed_text":  "Day 1 â€” Looking at the industry differently:\nWe explored Instagram\u0027s recommendation algorithm and a Design Thinking activity that encouraged us to approach problems from different perspectives. We also studied the evolution of a retail sector, with our team choosing the mobile sector for further exploration.\n\nDay 2 â€” Understanding the sector:\nWe learned to create a Power BI dashboard and explored why our chosen sector matters. We then analysed the mobile retail sector through its value chain and SWOT analysis.\n\nDay 3 â€” A pause to process:\nA break from the structured sessions gave us time to reflect and build on what we had explored so far.\n\nDay 4 â€” Behaviour, technology and professional presence:\nWe were introduced to Prospect Theory and explored digital portfolios using Antigravity, GitHub, and Vercel, connecting technology with our professional identity.\n\nDay 5 â€” Exploring AI and new industries:\nWe explored Base44 as an AI app-building tool and discussed the importance of goals and vision. We also gained exposure to the agriculture and textile sectors, broadening our perspective beyond mobile retail.\n\nWeek 1 Takeaway:\nWeek 1 brought together industry understanding, design thinking, data, technology, and decision-making â€” helping us see that understanding the problem comes before building the solution.",
